# Restrict the build context to backend source and dependency metadata.
# Azure builds must not receive local data or evaluation files.
# The default exclusion also protects future files.
# Only the entries below are needed by the Dockerfile.
# Real environment files are excluded by the default.
# Git metadata is excluded by the default.
# Test fixtures are excluded by the default.
# Frontend files are excluded by the default.
# Model caches are excluded by the default.
# Local Python environments are excluded by the default.
# Downloaded tooling is excluded by the default.
# Documents are excluded by the default.
# Build outputs are excluded by the default.
# Logs are excluded by the default.
# The lockfile fixes dependency versions.
# The project metadata supplies dependency declarations.
# The README is referenced by project metadata.
# The app directory contains FastAPI application code.
# Its package subdirectories are included recursively.
# The Dockerfile itself is handled by Docker.
# This allowlist applies only to the image build context.
# It does not replace Git ignore rules.
# It does not grant access to Azure secrets.
# Azure injects configuration at runtime.
# Supabase remains the durable data store.
# No uploads should be stored in the image.
# No credentials should be stored in the image.
# Keep this list narrow when adding files.
# Review new backend files before adding exceptions.
# Local scripts are not part of the runtime.
# Database migrations are applied separately.
# The frontend is built separately on Vercel.
# Run builds from the repository root.
# This file cannot remove historical Git commits.
# Check Git history separately before publishing.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!app/
!app/**/
!app/**/*.py
**/.env*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
